.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-key-import 1  "tapectl-key-import " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-key\-import \- Import a public key from a file, or adopt an existing one as the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl key import\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR] [\fB\-\-alias\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-type\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import a public key from a file, or adopt an existing one as the permanent escrow recipient with \-\-escrow (ADR\-0005)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR \fI<TENANT>\fR
Tenant name (required unless \-\-escrow)
.TP
\fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Key alias (required unless \-\-escrow)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-type\fR \fI<KEY_TYPE>\fR [default: primary]
Key type
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-escrow\fR
Adopt this public key as the permanent escrow recipient (ADR\-0005). Refuses if one is already registered
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to public key file — or, with \-\-escrow, either a path or the literal age1... public key
